  "body": "## Why five builds failed to fix this\n\nEvery previous fix targeted a **crash**. v1.10.18 added a render boundary. v1.10.19 added a global fatal shield. v1.10.20 added a persistent crash log that survives a JS teardown.\n\nAll three stayed completely silent. That is the answer: **nothing was ever throwing.** There is no crash to catch. The app was rendering *nothing at all*.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`app/(tabs)/(home)/` contains only `_layout.tsx` and `home.tsx` — there is **no `index` route**.\n\nThe group resolved its entry screen through:\n\n```ts\nexport const unstable_settings = { initialRouteName: 'home' };\n```\n\nThis project runs **expo-router 6.0.24**. In Expo Router v6 that key was renamed from `initialRouteName` to **`anchor`** (expo/expo#28644). The old key is silently ignored — no warning, no error.\n\nSo the `(home)` group had **no index route and no honoured anchor**. Resolving `/(tabs)` or `/(tabs)/(home)` produced a navigator with **no screen to render**.\n\nA navigator that renders nothing throws nothing. The root view stays at its dark background colour, the Android Activity stays alive, the system bars keep drawing. Black screen, no error, no crash dialog, no logs.\n\nThat is why every error boundary, the fatal shield and the crash log all reported nothing: **they were all working correctly. There was simply no error.**\n\n## The fix\n\n1. `(tabs)/(home)/_layout.tsx` now declares `anchor: 'home'` (both keys kept for safety).\n2. `(tabs)/_layout.tsx` now declares `unstable_settings` with `anchor: '(home)'` — the `initialRouteName` prop on `<Tabs>` is a React Navigation prop and is **not** how expo-router picks a group's entry route.\n\n## Blank screen watchdog\n\nErrors were already handled. \"Renders nothing\" was silent — so it is now instrumented.\n\nScreens report a successful paint. If nothing paints within 8 seconds, the app shows **\"Screen failed to load\"** with the current route, the last screen that painted, the build stamp, and two working recovery buttons (Go to Home / Back to Login).\n\nA route that resolves to nothing can never again show as a plain black screen.\n\n## Regression tests\n\nNew `__tests__/route-anchor-black-screen.test.ts` — 7 tests, all passing:\n\n- both layouts declare a valid `anchor`\n- the anchor target route file exists\n- **every** route group under `(tabs)` resolves via an index route or an anchor\n- the post-login target resolves to a real file\n- the watchdog is mounted and screens report paint\n\nThe generic group test means adding a future group with no resolvable entry route **fails the build** instead of shipping a black screen.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `runChecks` (TypeScript + lint + structure): **0 errors**\n- New route tests: **7 pass / 0 fail**\n- Full suite: 1136 pass, 3 pre-existing unrelated failures\n- Gradle: `BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 4m 37s` (full clean build, 466 tasks)\n\nVerified in the shipped `index.android.bundle`: `Screen failed to load`, `blank-screen-watchdog`, `markScreenPainted`, `1.10.21 (119)`, plus the retained `IVX Runtime Error`, `Previous Crash Detected` and `IVX Render Error` layers.\n\nversionName 1.10.21 / versionCode 119\nSHA256: `794896fd48e18c440d76b52d6985f25b26b5c641b839b9c9b0d77e7ba8882723`"
